{
  "_about": "Which packaging an app may come in. Each app is installed ONE way: use=flatpak means the Flatpak is the app and its RPM/AppImage cannot be installed; use=rpm means the RPM is the app and its Flatpak cannot be installed. Enforced by cosmos_app_policy.py (dnf excludepkgs, a Flathub remote filter, the never-type-sudo wrapper and CosmOS Shop). To add an app: add an entry here, then move it in the Containerfile accordingly (test_cosmos_app_policy.py checks they agree). 'blocked' lists things that can never be installed in any form (terminal emulators). An entry with 'pack' is a Flatpak that is not in the base image but in that Expansion Pack (expansion-packs.json). 'dnf_only' groups may be installed as packages but not as Flatpaks or AppImages (game store clients).",
